      "value": "1"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "rosella aero build-up from AeroSandbox (combined). Moments about the MRP (the mass CG). Method combined. Trim point of the cruise_trim job (AeroBuildup of the tree): V 18.8445 m/s, alpha 0.0526 deg, elevator 2.1999 deg. Trim check: the method has the CL and Cm of that trim at alpha 1.4373 deg and elevator 6.7144 deg. The difference is the gap between the two methods. Limits: no propeller slipstream. AeroBuildup gives the bodies no rate effect. The combined method has the inviscid lifting-surface CL0 of the vortex lattice (no viscous lift loss). Aileron and rudder are 0 at the trim. CD0 and K come from the AeroBuildup polar, not from the method of the derivatives."
    }
  },
